2026-10-22T16:25:00Z  NOTE     The pre-queue architecture is the reference: at 6177f82 `AudioEngine::processAudioBuffer` emitted `pcmReceived`, `AudioController` called `VisualizerWindow::feedAudio` (mutex + vector under audioMutex_), and the render frame fed `min(framesToFeed, available)` to projectM. The current design pops the same per-frame batch from `AudioQueue`. Same semantics, so the defect is in the wiring or the queue identity, not the design.
2026-10-22T16:25:00Z  CHANGE   VisualizerRenderer::renderFrame now logs one INFO when the first PCM batch reaches projectM, and at most one WARN per ~10 s while the viz queue stays empty, carrying queue depth, dropped-frame count and the queue's rate. That separates the only three possible causes: producer never pushed (depth 0/dropped 0), nobody draining this queue (depth>0 with drops), or the renderer holding a different queue than the engine (depth 0 while audio plays).
